@model List<BlogPost>

@{
	ViewData["Title"] = "Home - TIIND";
}
<hr />
<div class="titleContainer">
	<h1 class="text-center mb-4">The Internet Is Not Dead</h1>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="text-block mb-4">
	According to most sources, The Dead Internet Theory is the belief that the vast majority of internet traffic, 
	posts and users have been replaced by bots and AI-generated content, and that people no longer shape the direction of the internet.
</div>
<div class="text-block mb-4">Before AI, before the dot com bubble burst, independant and personal websites flourished. Creatives used their sites a
	way of  expression, connection, and in some cases rebellion.
</div>
<div class="text-block mb-4">Now, a whole new generation is discovering this forgotten liberty through the "IndieWeb", a community of people building software to enable personal 
	independently hosted websites, to maintain their social data on their own web domains rather than on large centralized social networking services.</div>
<div class="text-block mb-4">Now enter this site, The Internet Is Not Dead, a forum dedicated to talking about all things amazing and awesome about the IndieWeb, technology, hacking
	and just down right cool stuff.
</div>
<div class="text-block mb-4"> So come on in, sit down, and connect with your fellow human.</div>
<div class="text-block mb-4 youtubeContainer">
	<iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/oYlcUbLAFmw?si=fj3sb1K1LdZv_itO" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0"
			allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
			referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="titleContainer">
	<h1 class="text-center mb-4">Recent Blog Posts</h1>
</div>
<hr />



@if (!Model.Any())
{
	<p class="text-center">No posts avalible yet</p>
}
else
{
	<div class="row cardContainer">
		@foreach (var post in Model)
		{
			@* <div class="cardContainer"> *@
				<div class="card h-100 w-100" style="max-width: 300px; height: 400px;">
					<div class="card-body d-flex flex-column">
						<h5 class="card-title">@post.Title</h5>
						<p class="text-muted">By @post.User.Name.ToString() on @post.PublishedDate.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd H:mm:ss")</p>
						<p class="card-text">
							@if (post.Content.Length > 100)
							{
								@post.Content.Substring(0, 100) <text>...</text>
							}
							else
							{
								@post.Content
							}
						</p>
						<div class="mt-auto">
							<a asp-controller="BlogPost" asp-action="Details" asp-route-id="@post.ID" class="btn btn-primary w-100">Read More</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			@* </div> *@
		}

	</div>
}